Author: Martin Vit <martin@voipmonitor.org>
Date:   Tue Sep 29 19:45:54 2026 +0000

    fix(scheduler): let decodes preempt in a prefill turn that scheduled nothing
    
    With prefill compute sharing, any waiting request counts as runnable
    prefill. While those requests cannot be admitted (every running slot is
    taken, or restores are waiting for GPU capacity), each contended step is
    a prefill turn, and running decodes get only the leftover pass, which
    may not preempt. When a decode needed a KV block from a full pool, that
    pass stopped without scheduling or preempting anything. The empty step
    left the fairness controller unchanged, so every later step was the same.
    Generation stopped with idle GPUs and no log lines until clients aborted
    the running requests (mrweiner: GLM-5.3-Flash TP2 with LMCache restore
    admission, four slots, KV cache at 98%).
    
    A prefill turn that scheduled nothing has no admitted work to protect,
    so its decode pass may now preempt, as in a decode turn.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py b/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
index 66bd89742..e9feff11a 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -2033,11 +2033,13 @@ class Scheduler(SchedulerInterface):
         # A prefill turn gives prefills first use of the model-step capacity.
         # Existing decodes then consume only capacity genuinely left over. New
         # requests admitted above are excluded by running_req_ids_at_step_start,
-        # so no request can be scheduled twice in one step.
+        # so no request can be scheduled twice in one step. A turn that
+        # scheduled nothing has no admitted work to protect; its decodes preempt
+        # as in a decode turn, or a full pool would leave every step empty.
         if adaptive_prefill_turn and token_budget > 0:
             schedule_running_requests(
                 "decode",
-                allow_preemption=False,
+                allow_preemption=not num_scheduled_tokens,
                 enforce_lora_limit=True,
             )
 
